From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 10:55:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] replay: log analysis guest writes at their instruction

A guest write made by an analysis callback during record/replay is one
EVENT_GUEST_WRITE in the log, at the instruction where the callback ran (the
event, the guest-write API and its layout map are in the engine/src overlay:
replay/replay-effect.c, panda/src/guest-write.c). Guest hypercalls are the
first site: one event per hypercall, answered or not. The new event shifts the
event numbering, so REPLAY_VERSION goes to 0xe02010.

The hypercall instructions of arm, aarch64, loongarch, mips, ppc and riscv
now start I/O (translator_io_start): under icount the instruction ends its
translation block, so the event is logged and read at an exact instruction
count, as for clock and random-number reads, and env changes take effect from
the next block. x86's hypercall is a port write, which already does.

Without TCG there is no replay engine: the guest-write scope is stubbed out
and refuses every write it would admit, env writes included.

meson.build generates the guest-write layout map for each softmmu target from
this build's debug info: panda/src/guest-layout-probe.c is compiled like the
target's files with -g, and panda/scripts/guest_layout.py reads CPUArchState
and the structs it points to from it with gdb, into
guest-layout-<target>.h, which guest-write.c includes. The layout depends on
the host (pthread sizes, which accelerators it builds), so no generated map
is committed.

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
Origin: new
---
 meson.build                                   | 21 ++++++++
 replay/replay-internal.h                      |  2 +
 replay/replay.c                               |  3 +-
 replay/stubs-system.c                         | 49 +++++++++++++++++++
 target/arm/tcg/translate-a64.c                |  1 +
 target/arm/tcg/translate.c                    |  1 +
 .../tcg/insn_trans/trans_extra.c.inc          |  1 +
 target/mips/tcg/translate.c                   |  1 +
 target/ppc/translate/fixedpoint-impl.c.inc    |  1 +
 target/riscv/tcg/translate.c                  |  1 +
 10 files changed, 80 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index 9c77219b727a61279925c4cd52b85c574c348a98..14133903562ee7b8d2891b6b48f56b3b3411bf67 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -4421,6 +4421,27 @@ foreach target : target_dirs
     lib_deps += dep.partial_dependency(compile_args: true, includes: true)
   endforeach
 
+  if get_option('panda') and target.endswith('-softmmu') and 'CONFIG_TCG' in config_target
+    # panda/src/guest-write.c's layout map, from this build's debug info: the probe is
+    # compiled like the target's files, with -g, and gdb reads its types
+    # (panda/scripts/guest_layout.py). The layout depends on the host, so it isn't committed.
+    guest_layout_probe = static_library('guest-layout-probe-' + target,
+                 sources: [files('panda/src/guest-layout-probe.c'), config_target_h[target],
+                           config_devices_h[target]] + genh,
+                 dependencies: lib_deps,
+                 include_directories: target_inc,
+                 c_args: c_args + ['-g', '-fno-eliminate-unused-debug-types'],
+                 build_by_default: false)
+    arch_srcs += custom_target('guest-layout-' + target + '.h',
+                 input: guest_layout_probe,
+                 output: 'guest-layout-' + target + '.h',
+                 command: [python, files('panda/scripts/guest_layout.py'),
+                           find_program('gdb'), '@INPUT@', '@OUTPUT@'],
+                 install: true,
+                 install_dir: get_option('includedir') / 'panda' / 'guest-layout')
+    c_args += ['-DGUEST_LAYOUT_H="guest-layout-@0@.h"'.format(target)]
+  endif
+
   lib = static_library('qemu-' + target,
                  sources: arch_srcs + genh,
                  dependencies: lib_deps,
diff --git a/replay/replay-internal.h b/replay/replay-internal.h
index fa94be90af6ae8c83bde51b47c63ec5713c6bfdb..7c8455c344791a93846cf96475f99f44343d8886 100644
--- a/replay/replay-internal.h
+++ b/replay/replay-internal.h
@@ -56,6 +56,8 @@ enum ReplayEvents {
     EVENT_AUDIO_IN,
     /* for random number generator */
     EVENT_RANDOM,
+    /* for guest writes made by analysis callbacks */
+    EVENT_GUEST_WRITE,
     /* for clock read/writes */
     /* some of greater codes are reserved for clocks */
     EVENT_CLOCK,
diff --git a/replay/replay.c b/replay/replay.c
index 0f65e6b85a8822aa8bb8bbdec860808d618f2eb5..7d72b42fb24c24e830f2fdd07c0024c7b724b9be 100644
--- a/replay/replay.c
+++ b/replay/replay.c
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@
 
 /* Current version of the replay mechanism.
    Increase it when file format changes. */
-#define REPLAY_VERSION              0xe0200f
+#define REPLAY_VERSION              0xe02010
 /* Size of replay log header */
 #define HEADER_SIZE                 (sizeof(uint32_t) + sizeof(uint64_t))
 
@@ -137,6 +137,7 @@ static const char *replay_event_name(enum ReplayEvents event)
         EVENT(AUDIO_OUT);
         EVENT(AUDIO_IN);
         EVENT(RANDOM);
+        EVENT(GUEST_WRITE);
 #undef EVENT
     default:
         if (event >= EVENT_ASYNC && event <= EVENT_ASYNC_LAST) {
